DECISION_VERSION 1.0.0

ID DECISION-0001

DATE 2026-07-25

STATUS APPROVED

OWNER President Cley Duarte

TITLE

PACE's business model: open-core engine, plus PACE Cloud (per-seat SaaS)
and Enterprise. The engine is free; the layer on top is paid.

CONTEXT

PACE must be monetizable (REQUEST-0007), but the CLI on its own cannot be
sold: it is free to run, easy to copy, and should be open to drive
adoption. Revenue must come from the layer above the engine, not the
engine itself.

DECISION

Open-core with four tiers:
  - CORE (free, open source): the CLI (init, context, doctor, create) and
    the local .pace/ memory. AI-agnostic, no account. Drives adoption.
  - PRO (~9 EUR / month): guided intake, managed per-chat memory, editor
    integrations (Cursor / Claude / Copilot).
  - TEAM (~19 EUR / user / month): PACE Cloud -- team sync, visual
    dashboard, cross-project search, roles and approvals. The main
    recurring revenue.
  - ENTERPRISE (custom): SSO, on-premise, audit, compliance, SLA.

PACE stays AI-agnostic (the user brings their own AI) -- no lock-in, a
selling point. Focus on B2B: teams and companies pay to not lose their
knowledge; solo developers rarely pay.

RATIONALE

Free core = low barrier and wide adoption; the paid value is team
collaboration, hosted AI-memory and governance -- exactly what a single
free CLI cannot provide. Validate demand (waitlist, interviews) before
building the paid cloud layer.

PROMOTED_FROM

REQUEST-0007

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
